{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21526406",
      "title": "Adding Basic Form Validation",
      "lectureOrder": 147,
      "videoOrder": 128,
      "sourceHash": "38f6bec801635cd14a7c29167b92dc9e4f5f0348d365761fa9507a2807545f86",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.06,
          "end": 4.763,
          "en": "So, now we know how to get values with v-model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.71,
          "end": 9.1,
          "en": "We also already saw that an alternative to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.1,
          "end": 10.47,
          "en": "could be refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.47,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "Refs behave differently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 14.56,
          "en": "but if you only want to read data once,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.56,
          "end": 16.423,
          "en": "they can be a great alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.71,
          "end": 19.87,
          "en": "Now I will stick to v-model here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.87,
          "end": 24.67,
          "en": "and I want to dive at least briefly into input validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.67,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "We already did some validation in the last course project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 33.07,
          "en": "where we showed this error alert if one input was empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.07,
          "end": 35.57,
          "en": "And of course that is something you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.57,
          "end": 38.07,
          "en": "In your submit method you can check all the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.07,
          "end": 42.35,
          "en": "and if some value doesn't satisfy some condition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.35,
          "end": 44.46,
          "en": "you want it to have satisfied,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 47.643,
          "en": "you can show an error alert, nothing wrong with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.34,
          "end": 53.499,
          "en": "We could also validate certain inputs on every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.499,
          "end": 56.3,
          "en": "or whenever the input blurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.3,
          "end": 58.927,
          "en": "For example, here on the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.927,
          "end": 62.2,
          "en": "we could watch for the blur event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.2,
          "end": 65.7,
          "en": "So, when the input loses focus, and then we could check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.7,
          "end": 68.5,
          "en": "if the value stored in there is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.5,
          "end": 71.853,
          "en": "And if it is not, we could show the user an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.51,
          "end": 75.49,
          "en": "Here's how we could implement this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.49,
          "end": 78.45,
          "en": "We can add a blur listener to the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 80.313,
          "en": "Blur is a built in event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.66,
          "end": 83.77,
          "en": "and we could then trigger a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.77,
          "end": 86.383,
          "en": "validateInput for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.25,
          "end": 91.15299999999999,
          "en": "which we add to our methods down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.22999999999999,
          "end": 97.63,
          "en": "Here, I'll add a new method, validateInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.63,
          "end": 100.763,
          "en": "And now we could add a new data property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.717,
          "end": 105.91,
          "en": "userNameValidity, which initially let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.91,
          "end": 108.82,
          "en": "is pending because we don't know it yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.82,
          "end": 111.77000000000001,
          "en": "The user didn't have a chance of entering anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.77000000000001,
          "end": 113.733,
          "en": "And here in validateInput,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.86,
          "end": 119.00999999999999,
          "en": "we could then check if this.username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.00999999999999,
          "end": 122.97,
          "en": "so the data property which we're updating with the model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 126.99,
          "en": "if this.username, once we trim it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.99,
          "end": 131.61,
          "en": "or we already trim up there with v-model as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 133.693,
          "en": "So, let's maybe do that so,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.693,
          "end": 137.13,
          "en": "that we don't need to do it again in the code down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.13,
          "end": 140.02,
          "en": "So, we check if this username is equal to an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.02,
          "end": 141.633,
          "en": "which means it would be invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.71,
          "end": 147.483,
          "en": "Then we can set this.usernameValidity to invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.99,
          "end": 153.12,
          "en": "Else, we set this.usernameValidity to valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 153.12,
          "end": 156.663,
          "en": "It's no longer pending because now we know that it is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.68,
          "end": 161.11,
          "en": "And with that, we could then for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.11,
          "end": 162.36,
          "en": "go up to the input again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.69,
          "end": 168.6,
          "en": "and add a paragraph below the labeled input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.6,
          "end": 172.233,
          "en": "where we say, please enter a valid name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 173.55,
          "end": 176.46,
          "en": "And we only show this with the if,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 176.46,
          "end": 181.46,
          "en": "if userNameValidity is equal to invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.85,
          "end": 184.553,
          "en": "So, not if it's pending and not, if it's valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 187.97,
          "end": 191.56,
          "en": "We could also add a conditional clause here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 191.56,
          "end": 193.7,
          "en": "to this form control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 193.7,
          "end": 197.07,
          "en": "Let's say we add an invalid class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.07,
          "end": 201.01,
          "en": "if userNameValidity is equal to invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 201.01,
          "end": 202.69,
          "en": "So if that yields true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 202.69,
          "end": 205.88,
          "en": "this invalid class is added to this div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 207.56,
          "end": 210.24,
          "en": "and we could utilize this in our CSS code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.24,
          "end": 212.27,
          "en": "here at the bottom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.27,
          "end": 216.4,
          "en": "For example here, to check if we have a form-control div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 216.4,
          "end": 218.94,
          "en": "which also has the invalid clause on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 220.3,
          "end": 223.808,
          "en": "and then target the input element in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 223.808,
          "end": 227.273,
          "en": "to give it a border color of red.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.31,
          "end": 232.98,
          "en": "And maybe repeat that rule here to all the target label",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 232.98,
          "end": 236.01,
          "en": "and give that a text color of red,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 236.01,
          "end": 238.133,
          "en": "to highlight the invalid input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 242.97,
          "en": "And if we do all of that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 242.97,
          "end": 244.71,
          "en": "it initially looks fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 244.71,
          "end": 246.43,
          "en": "But if you click in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 246.43,
          "end": 248.43,
          "en": "and then don't enter anything valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.43,
          "end": 251.97,
          "en": "and click out of there, it gets this blur event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 251.97,
          "end": 256.57,
          "en": "And hence we get our error message and our error styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 256.57,
          "end": 258.5,
          "en": "And if we enter something valid here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258.5,
          "end": 261.98,
          "en": "and then blur it again, we remove that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 261.98,
          "end": 263.65,
          "en": "And if we enter a bunch of white space",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 263.65,
          "end": 265.51,
          "en": "that also gets this styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.51,
          "end": 267.523,
          "en": "because we have the trim modifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 268.97,
          "end": 272.3,
          "en": "And that's just one idea I want to give you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 272.3,
          "end": 274.29,
          "en": "There are thousands of different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 274.29,
          "end": 276.09000000000003,
          "en": "of implementing validation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 276.09000000000003,
          "end": 278.21,
          "en": "and you can also definitely implement it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.21,
          "end": 282.14,
          "en": "in a more flexible and dynamic way than I did it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 282.14,
          "end": 285.04,
          "en": "But it is important to be aware of patterns like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 285.04,
          "end": 287.276,
          "en": "since this allows you to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.276,
          "end": 291.09000000000003,
          "en": "the user interfaces and user experiences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 291.09000000000003,
          "end": 294.59000000000003,
          "en": "you probably want to offer to your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.59000000000003,
          "end": 296.9,
          "en": "So, that's it for now about validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.9,
          "end": 300.99,
          "en": "One possible way of adding live validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.99,
          "end": 302.9,
          "en": "before something is submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 302.9,
          "end": 305.13,
          "en": "not that the other approach would be wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 307.26,
          "en": "but just to also show this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 307.26,
          "end": 310.883,
          "en": "now, let's see how we can build our own form controls.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
